  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $85.9M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Energy recorded 104 awards with an average award size of $826K. Obligations fell 99.8% year over year. Fiscal obligations in prior years were $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, $48.5B in FY25, and $55.1B in FY26. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the dominant category in FY2027 to date with $81.1M in obligations. Remediation Services is the second category with $5.1M. The top vendor is UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC with $81.1M, followed by HANFORD LABORATORY MANAGEMENT AND INTEGRATION LLC with $7.5M. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and the page notes that all figures are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the scale and trend of Energy's contracting in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $85.9M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.8% year over year compared with prior fiscal years. The Department of Energy recorded 104 awards and an average award size of $826K. Fiscal obligations in recent years were $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, $48.5B in FY25, and $55.1B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors received the most contract dollars?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $81.1M in FY2027 to date. Remediation Services received $5.1M, and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services received $96.9K. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC received $81.1M and HANFORD LABORATORY MANAGEMENT AND INTEGRATION LLC received $7.5M, with BOOTH MANAGEMENT CONSULTING, LLC at $96.9K and TPGI CPA PLLC at $48.2K."
      }
    ]
